# 2026-09-18. Gated on verify PASS (hash ad96f882becbee92, 22 experiments, 7.9 min).
#
# `rel100-250` (jump 1.00, tau 250, hc 0.60) reached anti-phase -0.217, 0/12 seeds
# degenerate, beating both its singles by >= 10 SE. The experiment printed
# "THE TWO HALVES TAKE TURNS". FIVE ATTACKS, AND IT FAILS ALL OF THEM:
#
# 1. THE RATE COLLAPSED. 0.54 Hz against a 4.93 baseline -- 9x DOWN. The kill switch
#    voided rate ABOVE 2.5x baseline and never checked BELOW, which is the
#    denominator-shrinking artefact this project's own pre-registrations keep naming.
#
# 2. THE PATTERN ACROSS ARMS IS SPARSITY. rel100-83 1.33 Hz (11/12 degenerate),
#    rel30 1.07 (11/12), rel100 0.76 (11/12), rel100-250 0.54 (0/12). Lower rate ->
#    fewer degenerate seeds -> more anti-phase. Two SPARSE trains that rarely overlap
#    are anti-correlated BY CONSTRUCTION, with no oscillator anywhere.
#
# 3. DECISIVE -- THE HALVES ARE WEAKER THAN THE WHOLE. -0.217 over the full record
#    against -0.178 / -0.138 within halves (mean -0.158). A stable alternation reads
#    the SAME in each half. A slow OPPOSING DRIFT -- one posture fading while the
#    other grows -- is more anti-correlated across the whole record than inside
#    either piece of it, which is exactly the ordering observed.
#
# 4. THE FREQUENCY DOES NOT TRACK tau_a. Exponent -0.121 against ~1.000 required.
#    The instrument's own pre-registered check flagged this in the printed output.
#
# 5. THE HALF-DIFFERENCE SPECTRUM IS NOT COMPELLING. half-diff SNR 5.66 +/- 0.80
#    against the ~3.9 argmax-of-22-bins null adaptclock measured: +2.2 SE, below this
#    project's 3 SE bar and inside its "hypothesis, not a finding" band.
#
# SO: NOT a clock, and probably not even alternation -- most likely drift plus
# sparsity in a population that adaptation has nearly switched off. The verdict is
# RETRACTED for the fourth time, but note what changed: attacks 3 and 4 came from
# quantities the instrument now prints itself.
#
# TWO INSTRUMENT REPAIRS MADE IN RESPONSE:
#   - the rate kill switch is now bounded on BOTH sides (voids below 0.40x baseline
#     as well as above 2.5x);
#   - the positive verdict is GATED ON A DRIFT CHECK: if the whole record is more
#     anti-correlated than the mean of its halves, it prints DRIFT and returns false.
#     This exact false positive can no longer print as a success.
#
# WHAT IS ESTABLISHED, and it is real:
#   - the shipped larynx's two F1 postures are POSITIVELY correlated, +0.367 +/- 0.009
#     (neither) and +0.342 (fatigue), 0/12 degenerate -- they move TOGETHER;
#   - mutual inhibition alone SETTLES: 11/12 seeds degenerate in every inhib arm,
#     which is Matsuoka's prediction confirmed;
#   - scoping adaptation to the competing populations lets the jump reach 1.00
#     (20x what muted the larynx) with duty 0.57 intact;
#   - but at that jump the group's rate collapses to 0.11x baseline, so the circuit
#     is in the FUSION/silence regime, not an oscillating one.
#
# THE NEXT STEP IS THE ONE WRITTEN DOWN TWICE AND STILL NOT RUN: per
# Shpiro/Curtu/Rinzel/Rubin the oscillating regime is a bounded window in INPUT
# STRENGTH with a winner-take-all gap in the middle, and the boundaries do NOT move
# with the time constants. Every run so far has swept tau and inhibition and left
# input strength at the shipped operating point. The rate collapse now makes this
# doubly clear: the drive to group 2 has to come UP to compensate the fatigue.
